  "mechanismSummary": "Warmed in water, the diazonium ion loses nitrogen gas, the best leaving group there is, giving a phenyl cation. This cation is so reactive that it takes the nearest nucleophile, water; loss of a proton gives phenol. Diazotisation followed by hydrolysis replaces an amino group on a ring by OH.",
